  <title>Frames, boxes and lines</title>

  <p><gui>+ Frame</gui> adds a box. A frame is also how to draw a straight
  horizontal or vertical rule (a frame a few dots tall or wide), and a solid
  black block.</p>

  <terms>
    <item>
      <title><gui>Width</gui> and <gui>Height</gui></title>
      <p>The outside of the frame, in dots.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><gui>Thickness</gui></title>
      <p>The border, drawn inward from the outside edge. At half the shorter
      side the border meets in the middle and the frame is solid black; the
      thickness cannot go past that.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><gui>Corner Rounding</gui></title>
      <p>0 for square corners, up to 8, the roundest the printer draws.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><gui>Colour</gui></title>
      <p><gui>Black</gui> or <gui>White</gui>.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><gui>Reverse</gui></title>
      <p>Turns whatever is already printed beneath the frame's border white,
      and the paper under it black, whatever the colour.</p>
    </item>
  </terms>

  <note>
    <p>A printer cannot print white: a <gui>White</gui> frame prints nothing
    on bare labels. It shows only where it lies over something black, and
    the canvas draws it that way.</p>
  </note>
</page>
